  <data name="Quote1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Discipline is choosing what you want most over what you want now.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You do not rise to the level of your goals. You fall to the level of your systems.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The work you skip today becomes the person you don’t trust tomorrow.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Start before you feel ready. Readiness is often just a delay.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A boring, repeated 25 minutes will beat a dramatic plan.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Don’t negotiate with the version of you that wants to quit.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Consistency is a kindness you do for your future self.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote8" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If it’s important, it gets a time slot — not a wish.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote9" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show up small. Stay long enough for it to compound.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Quote10" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Today only asks for the next honest block of focus.</value>
  </data>
